      },
      {
        "title": "Education and early company chronology",
        "text": "The university records biomedical-science study, a PhD in Cancer Biology at the Institute of Cancer Research in London, and an academic appointment at the University of Miami. Its historical account places Science Exchange in Y Combinator’s 2011 program. The article’s leadership and financing details describe that period; they should not be treated as a current executive roster or valuation.",
